-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       The Simpsons: Bart vs. the Space Mutants, level 2
  Publisher   Ocean, 1991
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Simpsons - Bart vs the Space Mutants (1991)(Ocean)[128K].tap
  MD5         8e08c32c3265f6c4a65cf7e5f72b9913

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The figures painted in the cartoon's colours (196 shapes of this
              level; a first pass). Off by default. A painted set, colourist
              not named.

  Pace        original

  Note        Level 2 of the tape's five, started from the tape's own load of
              it with no loading. Every moving figure is a hardware sprite
              laid on its own pixels; the game underneath is unchanged.
              Enhanced paints the figures in the cartoon's colours. At the end
              of the level the game asks for the tape: start the next level's
              patch instead. Known issues: a few shapes no recording drew stay
              unpainted; figures cut off by the top of the play area keep the
              scenery's colours.

